  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the role of corporate sector in safeguarding UNESCO World Heritage sites</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNESCO has closely worked with the corporate sector for more than two decades to ensure that companies avoid damage to UNESCO-designated World Heritage sites from their business operations. This work has resulted in global standards on corporate sustainability developed by UNESCO, and more than 50 major public and private companies, industry associations and other corporate sector stakeholders across the various sectors taking a commitment to protect UNESCO World Heritage sites. Building on these achievements, the project focuses on further stimulating the uptake of such commitments by the corporate sector. See more at https://whc.unesco.org/en/no-go-commitment.</narrative>
  </description>
